<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-1">1 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Lincoln's Emancipation Proclamation comes into force</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abraham-lincoln">Abraham Lincoln</a>'s proclamation declared enslaved people in the rebelling Confederate states free. It turned the Civil War into a war against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> and opened the Union army to Black soldiers.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-2">2 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Union holds the field at the Battle of Stones River</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A failed Confederate assault on the final day of fighting near Murfreesboro, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tennessee">Tennessee</a>, led Braxton Bragg to withdraw. The costly Union success lifted Northern morale after the defeat at Fredericksburg.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-17">17 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Committee that became the Red Cross meets in Geneva</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Five Genevans, including Henri Dunant, founded a committee to aid wounded soldiers, inspired by Dunant's account of Solferino. It became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/international-committee-of-the-red-cross">International Committee of the Red Cross</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-2">2 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Stonewall Jackson is shot by his own men at Chancellorsville</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Returning from a night reconnaissance, General Thomas 'Stonewall' Jackson was hit by fire from Confederate pickets. He died of pneumonia eight days later, a grave loss to Lee.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-10">10 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Stonewall Jackson dies of pneumonia</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Eight days after being wounded by his own men at Chancellorsville, General Thomas 'Stonewall' Jackson died. Lee said he had lost his right arm.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-1">1 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Battle of Gettysburg begins in Pennsylvania</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Confederate and Union forces collided at Gettysburg, opening the largest battle ever fought in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>. Three days later Lee's army withdrew, having suffered some 23,000 of the roughly 50,000 casualties.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-2">2 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Union troops hold Little Round Top on Gettysburg's second day</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Confederate assaults struck the Union left at Little Round Top, the Wheatfield and the Peach Orchard. The Union line held its high ground by a narrow margin, setting the stage for Pickett's Charge the next day.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-3">3 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Pickett's Charge fails on the final day of Gettysburg</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Some 12,500 Confederates advanced across open fields against the Union centre on Cemetery Ridge and were cut down. The repulse ended Lee's invasion of the North and is often called the high-water mark of the Confederacy.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-4">4 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Vicksburg surrenders to Ulysses S. Grant</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">After a 47-day siege, John Pemberton surrendered Vicksburg and nearly 30,000 men. With Port Hudson falling days later, the Union controlled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> and split the Confederacy in two.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-18">18 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The 54th Massachusetts leads the assault on Fort Wagner</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The 54th Massachusetts, one of the first Black regiments in the Union army, led a night attack on Fort Wagner near Charleston. The assault failed with heavy losses, but the regiment's courage changed Northern opinion.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-3">3 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Lincoln proclaims a national day of Thanksgiving</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Amid the Civil War, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abraham-lincoln">Abraham Lincoln</a> proclaimed the last Thursday of November a national day of thanksgiving. The proclamation answered years of campaigning by the editor Sarah Josepha Hale and began an annual federal holiday.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-27">27 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Union forces win the Battle of Brown's Ferry near Chattanooga</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Union forces led by General William Farrar Smith defeated Confederate forces at Brown's Ferry in Hamilton County, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tennessee">Tennessee</a>, opening a supply line to the besieged city of Chattanooga.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-29">29 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">A Geneva conference founds the Red Cross movement</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">An international conference called by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva">Geneva</a> committee of Henri Dunant closed by adopting resolutions for national relief societies for wounded soldiers. The Red Cross movement and the 1864 Geneva Convention followed.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-19">19 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Lincoln delivers the Gettysburg Address</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At the dedication of the Soldiers' National Cemetery, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abraham-lincoln">Abraham Lincoln</a> spoke for about two minutes. His short address recast the Civil War as a struggle for 'a new birth of freedom' and government 'of the people'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-25">25 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Union troops storm Missionary Ridge</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At Chattanooga, Union soldiers charged up Missionary Ridge beyond their orders and routed Braxton Bragg's Confederate army. The victory opened the way into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-coche" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-coche.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-coche">Treaty of Coche</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty of Coche was the agreement signed in April 1863 at the Coche estate near Caracas that ended the Federal War in Venezuela.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-rangiriri" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-rangiriri.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-rangiriri">Battle of Rangiriri</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Rangiriri was fought on 20–21 November 1863 in the Waikato, New Zealand, during the British invasion of the Waikato.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-vicksburg" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/siege-of-vicksburg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Siege</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-vicksburg">Siege of Vicksburg</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Siege of Vicksburg, from May to 4 July 1863, ended with the surrender of the Confederate fortress on the Mississippi River in Mississippi to Union forces under Ulysses S.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt-congress-of-princes">Frankfurt Congress of Princes</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Frankfurt Congress of Princes was a meeting of German sovereigns convened by Emperor Franz Joseph of Austria in Frankfurt in August 1863 to approve an Austrian plan for reforming the German Confederation.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/rionegro-convention">Rionegro Convention</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Rionegro Convention was the constituent assembly that met at Rionegro, Antioquia, in 1863 after the Liberal victory in the Colombian civil war of 1860–1862.</p></div></li></ol></section>
